 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the executive law, in relation to adding the Roeliff Jansen Kill to the definition of inland waterways",
    "basePrintNo": "S6329",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6329-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §911, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6329\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the executive law, in relation to adding the Roeliff\nJansen Kill to the definition of inland waterways\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nTo designate the Roeliff Jansen Kill as an Inland Waterway for purpose\nof the State's Coastal and Inland Waterways program.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nThis bill amends Subdivision 4 of section 911 of the Executive Law by\nexpanding the definition of \"inland waterways\" to include the Roeliff\nJansen Kill.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe Roeliff Jansen Kill is a 56.2 mile long waterway which flows\nbetween Southern Columbia County and Northern Dutchess County before\nfeeding into the Hudson River. The New York State Department of\nEnvironmental Conservation has classified the Roeliff Jansen Kill as a\ncold-water habitat having conditions suitable for trout or trout\nspawning. The town of Copake's 2011 Comprehensive Plan recognizes that\nthe \"management of all water resources is a top priority in Copake.\"\n\nThe Columbia Land Trust has designated the Roeliff Jansen Kill as a\npotential water trail in their Harlem Rail Trail project. The stream\ntravels though two public parks. In Columbia County it flows through\nthe 330 acre Roeliff Jansen Park in Hillsdale. In Dutchess County it\nflows through the Roeliff Jansen Kill Multi Use Area coving 128 acres\nin the town of Milan. These parks provide trails and developed\nwaterfront. Still, many more miles remain undeveloped presenting\nsignificant potential for increased public access and use.\n\nDesignating the Roeliff Jansen Kill as an inland waterway would allow\nthe town of Copake to apply for grants though the Local Waterfront\nRevitalization Program. These grants will help in Copake's plan to\nimplement local waterfront revitalization programs to foster the\nbeneficial use of the waterfront and to protect and preserve the\nhealth and quality of the Roeliff Jansen Kill for the residents of\nCopake, the County of Columbia, and the State of New York.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone to the Senate.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
